      "text": "At 07:58:53 local time (UTC+7), a major undersea earthquake with a magnitude of 9.2–9.3 Mw struck off the west coast of northern Sumatra, Indonesia. Known as the Sumatra–Andaman earthquake, it was caused by a rupture along the fault between the Burma plate and the Indian plate."
