      "headline": "Global Impact",
      "text": "The tsunami affected 14 countries, including Thailand, Sri Lanka, India, and the Maldives, causing widespread devastation and loss of life."
    },
    {
      "date": "2004-12-26",
      "headline": "Humanitarian Response",
      "text": "The disaster prompted a massive international humanitarian response, with numerous countries and organizations providing aid and support to the affected regions."
    },
    {
      "date": "2004-12-26",
      "headline": "Death Toll",
      "text": "The disaster resulted in an estimated 230,000 to 280,000 deaths, making it one of the deadliest natural disasters in recorded history."
    },
    {
      "date": "2005",
      "headline": "Reconstruction Efforts",
      "text": "In the aftermath, affected countries began extensive reconstruction efforts, with international aid playing a significant role in rebuilding infrastructure and communities."
    },
