      "date": "1954-11-03",
      "headline": "Release of the First Godzilla Film",
      "text": "The original 'Godzilla' film, directed by Ishirō Honda and produced by Toho Co., Ltd., was released in Japan. It introduced the iconic monster Godzilla, a prehistoric reptilian creature awakened and empowered by nuclear radiation."
    },
    {
      "date": "1955-04-24",
      "headline": "Release of 'Godzilla Raids Again'",
      "text": "The second film in the franchise, 'Godzilla Raids Again', was released. It featured the first appearance of another kaiju, Anguirus, and established the concept of Godzilla battling other monsters."
    },
    {
      "date": "1962-08-11",
      "headline": "Release of 'King Kong vs. Godzilla'",
      "text": "This film marked the first crossover between Godzilla and another iconic monster, King Kong. It became a major box office success and further popularized the Godzilla franchise."
    },
    {
      "date": "1964-04-29",
      "headline": "Release of 'Mothra vs. Godzilla'",
      "text": "This film introduced Mothra, another popular kaiju, into the Godzilla series. It is considered one of the classic entries in the franchise."
    },
    {
      "date": "1968-08-01",
      "headline": "Release of 'Destroy All Monsters'",
      "text": "This film featured an ensemble cast of kaiju, including Godzilla, Mothra, Rodan, and King Ghidorah, among others. It was initially intended to be the final Godzilla film."
    },
    {
      "date": "1971-12-17",
      "headline": "Release of 'Godzilla vs. Hedorah'",
      "text": "Known for its environmental message, this film introduced Hedorah, a pollution-based monster, and reflected the growing environmental concerns of the time."
    },
    {
      "date": "1975-03-15",
      "headline": "Release of 'Terror of Mechagodzilla'",
      "text": "This film marked the end of the original Showa era of Godzilla films. It featured the return of Mechagodzilla and introduced the monster Titanosaurus."
    },
    {
      "date": "1984-12-15",
      "headline": "Release of 'The Return of Godzilla'",
      "text": "This film rebooted the Godzilla series, ignoring all previous sequels to the 1954 original. It began the Heisei era of Godzilla films."
    },
    {
      "date": "1995-12-09",
      "headline": "Release of 'Godzilla vs. Destoroyah'",
      "text": "This film concluded the Heisei era of Godzilla films with the death of Godzilla, who succumbs to a nuclear meltdown."
    },
    {
      "date": "1998-05-20",
      "headline": "Release of the American 'Godzilla' Film",
      "text": "Directed by Roland Emmerich and produced by TriStar Pictures, this was the first American Godzilla film. It received mixed reviews but was a commercial success."
    },
    {
      "date": "1999-12-11",
      "headline": "Release of 'Godzilla 2000: Millennium'",
      "text": "This film began the Millennium era of Godzilla films, which featured standalone stories rather than a continuous narrative."
    },
    {
      "date": "2004-12-04",
      "headline": "Release of 'Godzilla: Final Wars'",
      "text": "Celebrating the 50th anniversary of Godzilla, this film featured numerous monsters from the franchise and was intended as a farewell to the series."
    },
    {
      "date": "2014-05-16",
      "headline": "Release of Legendary Pictures' 'Godzilla'",
      "text": "Directed by Gareth Edwards, this film marked the beginning of the MonsterVerse, a series of American films featuring Godzilla and other kaiju."
    },
    {
      "date": "2016-07-29",
      "headline": "Release of 'Shin Godzilla'",
