      "text": "Louis XIV was born on September 5, 1638, at the Château de Saint-Germain-en-Laye, France, to Louis XIII and Anne of Austria."
    },
    {
      "date": "1643-05-14",
      "headline": "Ascension to the Throne",
      "text": "Louis XIV became King of France at the age of four upon the death of his father, Louis XIII. His mother, Anne of Austria, served as regent during his minority."
    },
    {
      "date": "1661-03-09",
      "headline": "Personal Rule Begins",
      "text": "Following the death of his chief minister, Cardinal Mazarin, Louis XIV decided to rule without a chief minister, marking the beginning of his personal reign."
    },
    {
