      "text": "Nebuchadnezzar II ascended to the throne, initiating a period of extensive building projects and military campaigns."
    },
    {
      "date": "-586",
      "headline": "Destruction of Jerusalem",
      "text": "Nebuchadnezzar II captured Jerusalem, destroyed the First Temple, and initiated the Babylonian Exile of the Jewish people."
    },
    {
      "date": "-539",
      "headline": "Fall of Babylon to Cyrus the Great",
      "text": "Cyrus the Great of Persia conquered Babylon, incorporating it into the Achaemenid Empire and ending the Neo-Babylonian Empire."
    },
    {
      "date": "-331",
      "headline": "Conquest by Alexander the Great",
      "text": "Alexander the Great captured Babylon, marking the beginning of Hellenistic influence in the region."
    },
    {
      "date": "-323",
      "headline": "Death of Alexander the Great",
      "text": "Alexander the Great died in Babylon, leading to the division of his empire among his generals."
    },
    {
      "date": "141",
      "headline": "Decline of Babylon",
      "text": "By this time, Babylon had significantly declined as a major urban center, overshadowed by the rise of other cities such as Seleucia."
    }
  ]
}

