      "headline": "Lunar Module Eagle Lands on the Moon",
      "text": "The Lunar Module Eagle, piloted by Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin, separated from the Command Module Columbia and landed on the Moon's surface at 20:17 UTC in the Sea of Tranquility."
    },
    {
      "date": "1969-07-21",
      "headline": "First Human Steps on the Moon",
      "text": "Neil Armstrong became the first human to step onto the Moon's surface at 02:56 UTC, famously declaring, 'That's one small step for [a] man, one giant leap for mankind.'"
    },
    {
      "date": "1969-07-21",
      "headline": "Buzz Aldrin Joins Armstrong on the Moon",
      "text": "Buzz Aldrin joined Neil Armstrong on the lunar surface 19 minutes after Armstrong's first step. Together, they conducted experiments and collected lunar samples."
    },
    {
      "date": "1969-07-21",
      "headline": "Exploration of Tranquility Base",
      "text": "Armstrong and Aldrin spent about two and a quarter hours exploring the lunar surface, conducting experiments, and collecting 47.5 pounds (21.5 kg) of lunar material."
    },
    {
      "date": "1969-07-21",
      "headline": "Lunar Module Lifts Off from the Moon",
      "text": "After spending 21 hours and 36 minutes on the lunar surface, the Lunar Module Eagle lifted off to rejoin the Command Module Columbia in lunar orbit."
    },
    {
      "date": "1969-07-24",
      "headline": "Apollo 11 Returns to Earth",
      "text": "Apollo 11 safely splashed down in the Pacific Ocean at 16:50 UTC, marking the successful completion of the mission and the safe return of astronauts Neil Armstrong, Buzz Aldrin, and Michael Collins."
