      "text": "The Mausoleum at Halicarnassus was built between 353 and 350 BCE in present-day Bodrum, Turkey. It was a tomb built for Mausolus, a satrap of the Persian Empire, and his wife, Artemisia II."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0435",
      "headline": "Completion of the Statue of Zeus at Olympia",
      "text": "The Statue of Zeus at Olympia was completed around 435 BCE by the sculptor Phidias. It was a giant seated figure of Zeus, made of ivory and gold-plated bronze, located in the Temple of Zeus in Olympia, Greece."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0450",
      "headline": "Construction of the Temple of Artemis at Ephesus",
      "text": "The Temple of Artemis at Ephesus, also known as the Artemision, was completed around 550 BCE. It was a large temple dedicated to the goddess Artemis, located in Ephesus (near modern-day Selçuk, Turkey)."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0560",
      "headline": "Construction of the Statue of Zeus at Olympia",
      "text": "The Statue of Zeus was constructed by the sculptor Phidias around 435 BCE. It was a monumental statue of the god Zeus, located in the Temple of Zeus at Olympia, Greece."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0600",
      "headline": "Construction of the Hanging Gardens of Babylon",
      "text": "The Hanging Gardens of Babylon are said to have been built in the ancient city-state of Babylon, near present-day Hillah, Babil, in Iraq. They were described as a remarkable series of tiered gardens containing a wide variety of trees, shrubs, and vines."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0600",
      "headline": "Construction of the Colossus of Rhodes",
      "text": "The Colossus of Rhodes was a statue of the sun god Helios, erected in the city of Rhodes, on the Greek island of the same name, by Chares of Lindos in 280 BCE. It was considered one of the tallest statues of the ancient world."
    },
    {
      "date": "-0256",
      "headline": "Completion of the Great Pyramid of Giza",
      "text": "The Great Pyramid of Giza, also known as the Pyramid of Khufu or the Pyramid of Cheops, was completed around 2560 BCE. It is the oldest and largest of the three pyramids in the Giza pyramid complex and the only one of the Seven Wonders still largely intact."
